@page "/mcp-server"

@* Describes the MCP server this demo's host maps at /mcp. Its route differs from the endpoint's on
   purpose: two literal endpoints on /mcp would make a GET of it ambiguous. *@

<PageTitle>MCP server - bit BbScanner</PageTitle>

<h1>MCP server</h1>

<p class="lede">
    This site hosts a Model Context Protocol server at <code>/mcp</code>, so an AI agent writing scanning code
    with Bit.BbScanner reads the library itself - its compiled API documentation, its guide, its symbology flags
    and option defaults, its decoder and these demo pages - instead of guessing at an API it half remembers.
    Every tool is read-only.
</p>

<div class="card">
    <h2 style="margin-block-start:0;">Connect a client</h2>

    <p>
        The endpoint is plain Streamable HTTP, so any MCP client connects with a URL and nothing else. The same tools
        are also served, version by version, through the bit platform's own server at
        <code>https://bitplatform.dev/mcp</code>, next to the other bit libraries.
    </p>

    <pre><code>@ClientConfig</code></pre>
</div>

<h2>Tools</h2>

<div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr><th>Tool</th><th>What it answers</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><code>SearchBbScanner</code></td>
                <td>Everything at once - the guide, every public member, the symbologies, the setup guides, the stylesheet and the demo sources - each hit with the exact follow-up call.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>GetBbScannerSetupGuide</code></td>
                <td>The complete wiring for one render mode: wasm, standalone-wasm, auto, server or hybrid.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>GetBbScannerGuideSection</code></td>
                <td>One section of the reference guide, or the index of sections.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>GetBbScannerApi</code></td>
                <td>One public type with every parameter, property and method, its real default and its documentation - or the index of types.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>GetBbScannerFormats</code></td>
                <td>The symbologies with their flags, what of each is read, whether the pipeline reads it, and the options that steer it with their real defaults.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>InspectBbScannerSymbol</code></td>
                <td>Renders a symbol, rotated and blurred if asked, decodes it with the library and returns the <code>BbBarcodeResult</code> it produced.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>GetBbScannerSourceFile</code></td>
                <td>One demo or library file verbatim - every page here is a working scanner - or the index of files.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

<p>
    The guide, the API, the symbologies and the sources are also exposed as <code>bbscanner://</code> resources, and
    three prompts - <code>add-bbscanner-to-app</code>, <code>implement-bbscanner-feature</code> and
    <code>debug-bbscanner</code> - walk an agent through the common jobs in the right order.
</p>

<h2>The same tools over plain HTTP</h2>

<p>
    Every tool is also a <code>GET</code> under <code>/api/mcp/...</code>: open one in a browser tab to read
    exactly what an agent is handed.
</p>

<ul>
    <li><a href="/api/mcp/SearchBbScanner?query=scan%20image%20file" target="_blank" rel="noopener">/api/mcp/SearchBbScanner?query=scan image file</a></li>
    <li><a href="/api/mcp/GetBbScannerApi?typeName=BbScanner" target="_blank" rel="noopener">/api/mcp/GetBbScannerApi?typeName=BbScanner</a></li>
    <li><a href="/api/mcp/GetBbScannerFormats?format=Ean13" target="_blank" rel="noopener">/api/mcp/GetBbScannerFormats?format=Ean13</a></li>
    <li><a href="/api/mcp/InspectBbScannerSymbol?format=QrCode&amp;rotation=30" target="_blank" rel="noopener">/api/mcp/InspectBbScannerSymbol?format=QrCode&amp;rotation=30</a></li>
    <li><a href="/api/mcp/GetBbScannerSourceFile?path=Demo/Client/Pages/Scan.razor" target="_blank" rel="noopener">/api/mcp/GetBbScannerSourceFile?path=Demo/Client/Pages/Scan.razor</a></li>
</ul>

